course: dictionary
lesson: 205
title: Alchemists: wizards or early scientists?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An alchemist was a person long ago, in the Middle Ages and before, who tried to turn ordinary metals like lead into gold. Many also searched for a medicine that would make people live for ever.
explain: Read this: «For centuries alchemists tried to turn lead into gold; they failed.» The word «failed» tells you the job could not be done, even though people tried for hundreds of years.
explain: In stories, an alchemist is a kind of wizard who mixes strange potions. Some people also call someone an alchemist when they seem to turn ordinary things into something wonderful.
explain: Alchemists never made gold, but their work helped chemistry begin. In history and science lessons they are the early form of chemists, the people who study what things are made of.
fact: An alchemist is a person who tried to turn ordinary metals like lead into gold.
fact: «Chinese alchemists discovered gunpowder, probably while looking for a medicine for long life.» Gunpowder was first used for fireworks and later in weapons.
fact: Alchemists invented many lab tools and methods, and they found out about many substances. This helped chemistry begin.
fact: The «philosopher's stone» was the magic stone that alchemists searched for.
fact: Chemistry cannot change one element into another, so alchemists could not turn lead into gold.
exercise: «For centuries alchemists tried to turn lead into gold.» What were alchemists trying to make? | Gunpowder for fireworks | Silk from spiders | *Gold from ordinary metal like lead
exercise: In stories, what is an alchemist? | A king | *A kind of wizard who mixes strange potions | A farmer | A ship captain
exercise: «Chinese alchemists discovered gunpowder.» What was gunpowder first used for? | Growing gardens | Cooking bread | *Fireworks
test: Someone who seems to turn ordinary things into something wonderful could be called an alchemist. What does this mean? | *They make ordinary things seem wonderful | They are a king of the Middle Ages | They literally turn things into gold
test: Did alchemists succeed in turning lead into gold? | Yes, but only in fantasy books | *No, they never did it | Yes, they made lots of gold
exam: In history and science lessons, what were alchemists? | Kings who ruled the Middle Ages | *The early form of chemists | Gold miners who dug in mountains | Pirates who sailed the seas
